	'book_0_a' => 'Arrive 5 minutes early so you can fill in the one-page form. It takes 5 minutes and asks where it hurts, when it started, and what makes it better or worse. Wear clothes you can move in, and bring shorts if the visit will look at a knee. The clinic is step-free, on the ground floor, at 14 Linden Row, Halbrook. Doors are open Monday to Friday from 08:00 to 19:30 and on Saturday from 08:30 to 13:00.',
	'book_0_b' => 'Sunday and public holidays are closed. The last first visit starts at 18:30 on a weekday and at 12:00 on Saturday, so a first visit has to be booked to begin by then. The phone desk is Monday to Friday, 08:00 to 18:00, on +00 44 555 0172. Evening slots from 17:00 to 19:30 are kept mainly for desk workers. Say if you are coming from the office. Email hello@teate-clinic.example is read when the desk is open.',
	'book_0_h' => 'Before you come',
	'book_1_a' => 'Four visits are the ones people ask for first, and the form lists them by name. A first visit is 60 minutes at EUR 95: talk, movement check, treatment and a plan. A follow-up is 40 minutes at EUR 70: treatment and a review of your exercises. A short follow-up is 25 minutes at EUR 50: one area, for returning patients. A sport check is 50 minutes at EUR 85: a running, cycling or swimming movement review and treatment.',
	'book_1_b' => 'The form also offers a workplace visit, 90 minutes at your office, desk set-ups for up to four people, at EUR 240. If you want five 40-minute follow-ups, that set is EUR 320 and is used within six months. Ask Inès Laurent to add it. Hands only: no machines, no ultrasound, no needles. Cancel up to 24 hours before at no cost. Many private health plans repay part of a visit; we give you a receipt to claim.',
	'book_1_h' => 'Prices you can book',
	'book_2_a' => 'Use the booking form on this page, or email hello@teate-clinic.example with the subject Booking request. Tell us where it hurts, which days suit you, and whether this is your first visit. Inès replies within one working day. The form asks for your name, email and phone, and for a visit type: first visit, follow-up, short follow-up, sport check or workplace visit. It asks where it hurts: neck and shoulders, lower back, sport niggle, or other.',
	'book_2_b' => 'You can choose Maren Holt, Kofi Mensah, or either. Preferred time is weekday morning, weekday afternoon, weekday evening or Saturday. There is room for a message about how the trouble started. You agree that Teate Clinic may contact you about this booking, and the button reads Send booking request. If the page gives you an email button instead, sending that message is the request. You are booked when Inès confirms the time.',
	'book_2_h' => 'Sending a booking request',
	'book_3_a' => 'Call +00 44 555 0172 during phone desk hours, Monday to Friday, 08:00 to 18:00. Inès Laurent answers and books every visit. Clinic hours run longer than the phone desk: Monday to Friday 08:00 to 19:30, Saturday 08:30 to 13:00, and closed on Sunday and public holidays. Outside phone desk hours, write to hello@teate-clinic.example and she will read it when the desk opens. Maren Holt is here on Monday, Tuesday, Thursday and Saturday.',
	'book_3_b' => 'Kofi Mensah is here on Monday, Wednesday, Thursday and Friday evenings. Ask for the person whose work matches yours, or ask for either. A first visit needs the full 60 minutes, so it starts no later than 18:30 on a weekday and no later than 12:00 on Saturday. Evening slots from 17:00 to 19:30 are kept mainly for people coming from work, which is worth saying when you call.',
