	'endonym' => 'English',
	'first-visit_0_a' => 'Book online, by phone on +00 44 555 0172, or by email at hello@teate-clinic.example. Tell Inès Laurent where it hurts and whether you would like to see Maren Holt or Kofi Mensah. Arrive 5 minutes early. The one-page form on the desk takes 5 minutes and covers where it hurts, when it started, and what makes it better or worse. Wear clothes you can move in. If the trouble is a knee, an ankle or a hip, shorts are the most useful thing you can bring.',
	'first-visit_0_b' => 'You stay dressed. The couch is low, and the room is step-free on the ground floor at 14 Linden Row, Halbrook. The last first-visit start is 18:30 Monday to Friday and 12:00 on Saturday. Evening slots from 17:00 to 19:30 are kept mainly for desk workers, so say if you are coming straight from the office. The phone desk is open Monday to Friday, 08:00 to 18:00.',
	'first-visit_0_h' => 'Before you come',
	'first-visit_1_a' => 'The first hour is paced the same way for every new patient, and the minutes are the method. Ten minutes are for talk: where it hurts, when, and what makes it better or worse. Fifteen minutes are for watching how you move, standing, sitting, bending and walking, with the osteopath\'s hands relaxed until they need to guide a movement. Twenty-five minutes are hands-on treatment on the couch. The last ten minutes are the plan, with two or three exercises to take home.',
	'first-visit_1_b' => 'That is 10 minutes, then 15, then 25, then 10, inside a 60-minute visit. The hour uses hands only: no machines, no ultrasound, no needles. Maren Holt usually leads this hour for neck, shoulder and lower-back trouble from desk work. Kofi Mensah leads it when you have come with a sport niggle. If fever, numbness, night pain or a fall means a doctor should see you first, we stop and say so.',
	'first-visit_1_h' => 'The hour',
	'first-visit_2_a' => 'You leave with a short plan, written in ordinary language. Many people need two to four follow-ups over a few weeks. Some need only one visit. We say so honestly, including when you do not need a string of appointments. The path into that plan is four plain steps. One: book online, by phone or email. Two: fill in the one-page form on arrival, which takes 5 minutes. Three: the first hour, as above.',
	'first-visit_2_b' => 'Four: a plan. A follow-up is 40 minutes at EUR 70, for treatment and a review of the exercises you were given. You can cancel up to 24 hours before at no cost. We give you a receipt. Many private health plans repay part of a visit; we give you a receipt to claim, and we leave the claim itself with you. Inès confirms the next time, if there is one, within one working day.',
	'first-visit_2_h' => 'After the visit',
	'first-visit_3_a' => 'The first visit is 60 minutes at EUR 95. What happens in that hour is the talk, the movement check, the treatment and the plan. The follow-up is 40 minutes at EUR 70: treatment and a review of your exercises. Those are the two prices most people use at the start. A short follow-up for returning patients, one area only, is 25 minutes at EUR 50 if a full follow-up is more than you need.',
	'first-visit_3_b' => 'A sport check is 50 minutes at EUR 85 when the reason for coming is running, cycling or swimming. Hands only: no machines, no ultrasound, no needles. Cancel up to 24 hours before at no cost. Many private health plans repay part of a visit; we give you a receipt to claim. If you already know you will be back several times, ask Inès about the set of five follow-ups when you book.',
	'first-visit_3_h' => 'The first two prices',
	'first-visit_h1' => 'First visit',
	'first-visit_lede' => 'A first visit is 60 minutes and costs EUR 95. It holds a talk, a look at how you move, hands-on treatment, and a plan you take home.',
