	'hero_h1' => 'Tell us where|it hurts.',
	'hero_lede' => 'Two osteopaths, one pale room in Halbrook, no machines. The first hour is mostly listening and watching how you move.',
	'hour_1_h' => 'Talk',
	'hour_1_p' => 'Where it hurts, when it started, and what makes it better or worse. Bring the ordinary week with you: the desk, the commute, the run, the move.',
	'hour_2_h' => 'Watching how you move',
	'hour_2_p' => 'Standing, sitting, bending and walking, in the pale room. This happens before any treatment.',
	'hour_3_h' => 'Hands-on treatment',
	'hour_3_p' => 'No machines, no ultrasound, no needles. You stay clothed. The couch is low, the linen is fresh, and the work is done with the hands.',
	'hour_4_h' => 'Plan and exercises',
	'hour_4_p' => 'Two or three exercises to take home. We show them once, you try them once, and you leave knowing when to do them.',
	'hour_book' => 'Book online, by phone on +00 44 555 0172, or by email at hello@teate-clinic.example. Inès Laurent books every visit. A follow-up is 40 minutes and EUR 70, and it reviews your exercises as well as treating.',
	'hour_h' => 'The first hour',
	'hour_intro' => 'The first visit is 60 minutes and costs EUR 95. Arrive five minutes early and fill in a one-page form. Wear clothes you can move in. If we are looking at a knee, wear shorts.',
	'hour_l' => 'THE HOUR',
