	'lang_label' => 'Language',
	'list_h' => 'Notes',
	'list_l' => 'NOTES',
	'list_p' => 'Short notes from Maren and Kofi, and changes to the hours, one clinic letter at a time.',
	'min' => 'min',
	'n1_by' => 'Maren Holt writes on the neck and the screen.',
	'n1_d' => '12 November 2026',
	'n1_t' => 'Three small changes at a desk that help a stiff neck',
	'n2_by' => 'Kofi Mensah writes for people who train for fun.',
	'n2_d' => '29 October 2026',
	'n2_t' => 'Building back after a knee niggle: notes for weekend runners',
	'n3_by' => 'No fee, no form: tell Inès by phone or email.',
	'n3_d' => 'Standing note',
	'n3_t' => 'Cancel up to 24 hours before at no cost',
	'newsletter_0_a' => 'Ruth Adeyemi, the practice manager, writes the clinic letter. Each month it carries three things. One exercise, something you can try at a desk or after easy training, described in plain language. Any change to the hours, which otherwise stay Monday to Friday 08:00 to 19:30, Saturday 08:30 to 13:00, and closed on Sunday and public holidays. And one short note from Maren Holt or from Kofi Mensah about the work they are seeing: necks and shoulders, lower backs, or sport niggles.',
	'newsletter_0_b' => 'The letter is a note from the practice to people who have asked for it. The exercise in the letter is general. The two or three exercises you are given in the room are chosen after someone has watched you move, and they belong to your plan. If the letter\'s exercise does not suit you, leave it out. The letter does not say that pain has been fixed, and it does not replace the first hour.',
	'newsletter_0_h' => 'What the letter holds',
	'newsletter_1_a' => 'Ask with the form on this page. The field is your email address, and the button says Get the clinic letter. The message goes to hello@teate-clinic.example with the subject Clinic letter: Teate Clinic. If the form opens your email app, your address is filled in for you. Send that message to ask for the letter. This opens your email app with your address filled in. Send it to ask for the clinic letter; you are not on the list until we reply.',
	'newsletter_1_b' => 'Inès Laurent or Ruth Adeyemi handles the reply, and the clinic\'s reply within one working day is the same standard as a booking message. You can also write to hello@teate-clinic.example yourself and say you would like the letter, naming the email that should receive it. We send it to people who have asked. The request means we may contact you about the letter. It does not book a visit, and it does not share your address with anyone outside the clinic.',
	'newsletter_1_h' => 'How to ask for it',
	'newsletter_2_a' => 'When the letter mentions a price, it uses the published list and no other. A first visit is EUR 95 for 60 minutes. A follow-up is EUR 70 for 40 minutes. A short follow-up is EUR 50 for 25 minutes. A sport check is EUR 85 for 50 minutes. Five follow-ups are EUR 320, used within six months. A workplace visit is EUR 240 for 90 minutes at your office, for up to four people. Hands only: no machines, no ultrasound, no needles.',
	'newsletter_2_b' => 'To stop the letter, write to hello@teate-clinic.example and say so. Inès takes the address off the list when she replies. Reading the notes on the website does not put you on the letter. Booking a visit does not put you on the letter either. The booking agreement covers that booking. The letter agreement covers the letter. Cancel a visit separately, up to 24 hours before, at no cost, on +00 44 555 0172 or by email.',
	'newsletter_2_h' => 'Prices, visits and stopping',
	'newsletter_h1' => 'Clinic letter',
	'newsletter_lede' => 'The clinic letter is a short monthly email from Teate Clinic: one exercise, any change to the hours, and a few lines from Maren Holt or Kofi Mensah.',
	'no_posts' => 'Nothing here yet.',
	'notices_all' => 'All notes →',
	'notices_h' => 'Notices',
	'notices_l' => 'NOTES',
