	'price_6_v' => 'Workplace visit',
	'price_6_w' => '90 minutes at your office, desk set-ups for up to four people',
	'prices_0_a' => 'The price list has six lines, and the same six lines are used everywhere on this site. First visit: talk, movement check, treatment and plan, 60 minutes, EUR 95. Follow-up: treatment and a review of your exercises, 40 minutes, EUR 70. Short follow-up: one area, for returning patients, 25 minutes, EUR 50. Sport check: a running, cycling or swimming movement review and treatment, 50 minutes, EUR 85.',
	'prices_0_b' => 'Five follow-ups: five 40-minute follow-ups, used within six months, EUR 320. Workplace visit: 90 minutes at your office, desk set-ups for up to four people, EUR 240. Hands only: no machines, no ultrasound, no needles. Cancel up to 24 hours before at no cost. Many private health plans repay part of a visit; we give you a receipt to claim. Inès Laurent reads the list out if you call +00 44 555 0172 during phone desk hours, Monday to Friday, 08:00 to 18:00.',
	'prices_0_h' => 'The six visits',
	'prices_1_a' => 'We give you a receipt after a visit so you can claim. Many private health plans repay part of a visit. The receipt is the document you send them. We do not send the claim for you, and we do not tell you that a particular plan will pay. The receipt shows the visit you had, the length and the amount in EUR. That amount is EUR 95, EUR 70, EUR 50, EUR 85, EUR 320 or EUR 240, matching the visit that was booked.',
	'prices_1_b' => 'It names the osteopath who treated you, Maren Holt or Kofi Mensah. Ask for it at the desk on the day, or write to hello@teate-clinic.example and Inès Laurent will help. The one-page form you fill in on arrival is for the clinic record. The receipt is the paper that leaves with you. Bring nothing extra for a claim beyond what your own plan has asked you to keep.',
	'prices_1_h' => 'Receipts',
	'prices_2_a' => 'Cancel up to 24 hours before at no cost. Tell Inès Laurent by phone on +00 44 555 0172 or by email at hello@teate-clinic.example. The phone desk is open Monday to Friday, 08:00 to 18:00, which is the reliable window for a change of plan. Saturday visits run from 08:30 to 13:00, so a message on Friday is the calm way to change a Saturday time.',
	'prices_2_b' => 'The last first visit still starts at 18:30 on a weekday and at 12:00 on Saturday, and a new booking has to fit those starts. Evening slots from 17:00 to 19:30 are kept mainly for desk workers, and Inès can offer one of those when you rebook if you are coming from the office. The same 24-hour rule covers a first visit, a follow-up, a short follow-up, a sport check, the five-visit set and a workplace visit.',
	'prices_2_h' => 'Cancelling',
	'prices_3_a' => 'Five follow-ups cost EUR 320. Each one is a 40-minute follow-up, the same kind of visit as a single follow-up: treatment and a review of your exercises. The five are used within six months. They are follow-ups, so they are not a first visit and they are not the 25-minute short follow-up. Many people need only two to four follow-ups over a few weeks, and some need only one.',
	'prices_3_b' => 'If you are unsure you will return, book single follow-ups at EUR 70 for 40 minutes, and decide after each plan. Inès Laurent notes the six-month window when you take the set. The set is hands-on care, with the same rule as every other visit. Hands only: no machines, no ultrasound, no needles. Cancel up to 24 hours before at no cost. A receipt is given so you can claim if your private health plan repays part of a visit.',
	'prices_3_h' => 'Five follow-ups',
	'prices_4_a' => 'A workplace visit is 90 minutes at your office, EUR 240, for desk set-ups for up to four people. It is for people who sit. Maren Holt is the osteopath whose daily work is the neck, shoulders and lower back of desk workers, and this visit is booked with that work in mind. For up to four people we look at the screen, the chair and the length of sitting, and we talk through two or three changes each person can keep.',
	'prices_4_b' => 'Four is the maximum on this price. Inès Laurent arranges the day and confirms it before anyone comes to you. Evening slots from 17:00 to 19:30 stay at 14 Linden Row for individual patients coming from work. The workplace visit is the one that travels to the office. Cancel up to 24 hours before at no cost. You receive a receipt for EUR 240. Hands only: no machines, no ultrasound, no needles.',
	'prices_4_h' => 'Workplace visit',
	'prices_h' => 'Prices',
	'prices_h1' => 'Prices',
	'prices_l' => 'EUR',
	'prices_lede' => 'Every visit at Teate Clinic is priced in EUR. The work in each of them is hands only: no machines, no ultrasound, no needles.',
	'prices_note' => 'Hands only: no machines, no ultrasound, no needles. Cancel up to 24 hours before at no cost. Many private health plans repay part of a visit; we give you a receipt to claim.',
	'privacy_0_a' => 'When you book, we ask for your name, email, phone number, visit type, where it hurts, a choice of clinician, a preferred time, a message if you want to add one, and your agreement that Teate Clinic may contact you about that booking. Visit types are a first visit, a follow-up, a short follow-up, a sport check or a workplace visit. Where it hurts is recorded as neck and shoulders, lower back, a sport niggle, or other. The clinician choice is Maren Holt, Kofi Mensah, or either.',
	'privacy_0_b' => 'Preferred times are weekday morning, weekday afternoon, weekday evening or Saturday. The contact form asks for your name, email, message, and your agreement that we may contact you about that message. The clinic letter asks for your email address. You can also call +00 44 555 0172 or write to hello@teate-clinic.example. The one-page form you fill in on arrival, which takes 5 minutes, stays with your visit notes at 14 Linden Row.',
	'privacy_0_h' => 'What you send us',
	'privacy_1_a' => 'Inès Laurent uses booking details to offer you a time and to reply within one working day. She uses a contact message to answer the question you asked. Ruth Adeyemi uses your email to send the clinic letter if you have asked for it, and only once we have replied to confirm you are on the list. If a form opens your email app, sending that email is your request. You are booked, or on the letter, only when we reply.',
	'privacy_1_b' => 'Maren Holt and Kofi Mensah see the notes they need in order to treat you in the room. A receipt for your visit, if you want to claim with a private health plan, shows the visit, the length, the amount in EUR and the osteopath\'s name. We give that receipt to you. We do not file the claim. Details you send are used for the visit, the reply or the letter you asked for. The clinic address for any of this is 14 Linden Row, Halbrook.',
	'privacy_1_h' => 'How we use it',
	'privacy_2_a' => 'The people who handle your details are the people who work at Teate Clinic. Inès Laurent, at the front desk, books every visit and answers the phone and the inbox. Ruth Adeyemi, the practice manager, writes the clinic letter. Maren Holt and Kofi Mensah, the osteopaths, write the clinical notes from your hour in the room. The clinic address is 14 Linden Row, Halbrook, and the email is hello@teate-clinic.example.',
	'privacy_2_b' => 'If you want to see what we hold, correct it, or ask us to stop contacting you, write to that address or call +00 44 555 0172 during phone desk hours, Monday to Friday, 08:00 to 18:00. Inès replies within one working day. Asking to stop the clinic letter is separate from a visit you have already booked. Cancelling a visit is its own message: up to 24 hours before, at no cost, by phone or by email to the same addresses.',
	'privacy_2_h' => 'Who sees your details',
	'privacy_3_a' => 'A booking agreement covers that booking. A contact agreement covers that message. A request for the clinic letter covers the letter. We keep the three apart so that asking a question does not subscribe you, and booking a visit does not add you to the letter. The notes on the website can be read without sending us your name. Hours, prices and the names of the clinicians are published so you can decide before you write.',
	'privacy_3_b' => 'We do not diagnose disease by form or by email. If you tell us about fever, numbness, night pain or a fall, we treat that as a reason to refer you to a doctor. Hands-on care pauses in those cases. This page is our privacy notice in plain language. If you need the same account in an email for your own records, write to hello@teate-clinic.example and ask Ruth Adeyemi. The hours, the prices and the people named here are the ones used in the clinic.',
	'privacy_3_h' => 'Bookings, letters and the website',
	'privacy_h1' => 'Privacy',
	'privacy_lede' => 'This page says what Teate Clinic does with the details you send when you book, write to us, or ask for the clinic letter. It is written in plain language for patients.',
	'prof_kofi_best' => 'Knees, ankles, runs and rides',
	'prof_kofi_best_l' => 'Best for',
	'prof_kofi_days' => 'Mon, Wed, Thu, Fri evenings',
	'prof_kofi_days_l' => 'Days',
	'prof_kofi_name' => 'Kofi Mensah',
	'prof_kofi_p' => 'Kofi Mensah is an osteopath and a co-founder of Teate Clinic. He treats sport niggles of the knees, ankles, hips and shoulders for runners, cyclists and swimmers who train for fun. He runs and cycles himself, so a question about a long run or a ride to work is a practical one. A sport check with him lasts 50 minutes: a movement review for running, cycling or swimming, then treatment. He will tell you if one visit is enough, and if you need a doctor instead.',
	'prof_kofi_role' => 'Osteopath, co-founder',
	'prof_maren_best' => 'Neck, shoulders, lower back',
	'prof_maren_best_l' => 'Best for',
	'prof_maren_days' => 'Mon, Tue, Thu, Sat',
	'prof_maren_days_l' => 'Days',
	'prof_maren_name' => 'Maren Holt',
	'prof_maren_p' => 'Maren Holt is an osteopath and a co-founder of Teate Clinic. She and Kofi Mensah met while working in a sports-club clinic, and in 2014 they opened this room together at 14 Linden Row. Maren treats the neck, shoulders and lower back of people who sit for their work. A first hour with her starts with where it hurts and how you move, then hands-on treatment, then a plan and two or three exercises. If what you tell her needs a doctor, she stops and refers you.',
	'prof_maren_role' => 'Osteopath, co-founder',
