	'sheet_label' => 'Where to start',
	'sheet_page' => 'On this page',
	'stories_0_a' => 'Daniel Okafor is an accountant. He came to Maren Holt with his neck after the year-end deadlines: stiffness, headaches at the end of the day, and a shoulder that sat up by the time he left the office. He began with a first visit and then returned. Across four visits over six weeks, Maren listened, watched how he sat and turned, treated with her hands, and sent him home with two exercises. They also changed his screen height.',
	'stories_0_b' => 'The room had a couch and linen, and the work stayed with the hands. The change he talks about is on the bike. He can check over his shoulder again without turning his whole body. That is his account of those six weeks. It is one person\'s experience. Another desk worker may need two to four follow-ups, or only one, and we say which it is after the first hour. Daniel needed four visits, then he stopped. Maren was his clinician throughout.',
	'stories_0_h' => 'Daniel Okafor, accountant',
	'stories_1_a' => 'Sofia Brandt is a weekend runner. The outside of her left knee had been nagging her, the kind of sport niggle Kofi Mensah sees in people who train for fun. She started with a sport check, a review of her running movement and treatment in the same visit, then three follow-ups. Kofi runs and cycles himself, and the plan stayed inside the running she already did. The long run built up more slowly. She added one strength session a week.',
	'stories_1_b' => 'She kept running. In the autumn she ran her half marathon at an easy pace. That is what Sofia did, told here as her experience. A runner, cyclist or swimmer with a knee, an ankle, a hip or a shoulder can book the same kind of start, the sport check, at 50 minutes. The number of follow-ups may be different from three. Kofi will say if one visit is enough. Her clinician for the sport check and the follow-ups was Kofi.',
	'stories_1_h' => 'Sofia Brandt, weekend runner',
	'stories_2_a' => 'Tomás Rivera is a designer. His lower back started after he moved house, with boxes to lift and a flat that still needed carrying. He saw Maren Holt for three visits. They worked on the back with the hands. He learned how to lift, and he learned how to break up long sitting, so the day was no longer one unbroken stretch in a chair. When the three visits were done, he went back to his work. He now comes back twice a year for a service.',
	'stories_2_b' => 'Those are his words, and twice a year is his choice. A priced set of five follow-ups exists for people who want five 40-minute visits inside six months. Tomás\'s course was three visits, and then the twice-yearly return. His complaint is the second of the three we see most: lower back from long sitting, lifting, moving house, or a sudden twinge. Maren was his clinician. If a fall, fever, numbness or night pain is part of your own story, we refer you to a doctor.',
	'stories_2_h' => 'Tomás Rivera, designer',
	'stories_3_a' => 'Every body is different; these are three people\'s experiences, not promises. Daniel Okafor, Sofia Brandt and Tomás Rivera were seen by Maren Holt or by Kofi Mensah in the room at 14 Linden Row, Halbrook. Their visits sat inside the same hours and the same price list as any other patient. A first visit is still 60 minutes at EUR 95. The pace inside it is still 10 minutes of talk, 15 minutes of watching you move, 25 minutes of hands-on treatment, and 10 minutes for a plan and two or three exercises.',
	'stories_3_b' => 'You book with Inès Laurent by phone on +00 44 555 0172, by email at hello@teate-clinic.example, or with the booking form. She replies within one working day. You can cancel up to 24 hours before at no cost. Hands only: no machines, no ultrasound, no needles. If you want to talk before you decide, the phone desk is open Monday to Friday, 08:00 to 18:00.',
	'stories_3_h' => 'Every body is different',
	'stories_h' => 'Three stories',
	'stories_h1' => 'Stories',
	'stories_l' => 'PROOF',
	'stories_lede' => 'Three people who came to Teate Clinic agreed we could describe what their visits were like. Names, complaints and the shape of each course of care are theirs.',
	'stories_more' => 'Read the stories →',
	'stories_note' => 'Every body is different; these are three people\'s experiences, not promises.',
	'story_daniel_by' => 'Clinician: Maren Holt',
	'story_daniel_ctx' => 'Daniel Okafor · Accountant · Neck',
	'story_daniel_h' => 'A neck after the year-end deadlines',
	'story_daniel_p' => 'His neck came on after the year-end deadlines, when the days at the desk ran long and looking over a shoulder had started to mean turning his whole body. Maren Holt saw him for four visits over six weeks. They changed the height of his screen, and he left with two exercises he could do away from the clinic. He can check over his shoulder on the bike again without turning his whole body. That is his account of those weeks. It is one person’s experience, not a promise.',
	'story_sofia_by' => 'Clinician: Kofi Mensah',
	'story_sofia_ctx' => 'Sofia Brandt · Weekend runner · Knee',
	'story_sofia_h' => 'The outside of a knee on the long run',
	'story_sofia_p' => 'The outside of her left knee had been nagging, and she wanted to keep training without guessing at the cause. Kofi Mensah began with a sport check and then saw her for three follow-ups. The long run built up more slowly, with one strength session a week beside it. She ran her autumn half marathon at an easy pace. Nothing here says the knee was cured. It says how her weeks were arranged, and that she finished at the pace they had chosen.',
	'story_tomas_by' => 'Clinician: Maren Holt',
	'story_tomas_ctx' => 'Tomás Rivera · Designer · Lower back',
	'story_tomas_h' => 'A back after moving house',
	'story_tomas_p' => 'His lower back started after he moved house, between the boxes and the lifting. Maren Holt saw him for three visits. He learned how to lift and how to break up long sitting, and he used both in the weeks after the move. He now comes back twice a year, in his own words, for a service. Three visits were what he needed then. Someone else, with another back and another move, may need a different number, and we say so when we see it.',
